The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'THELOOK_ECOMMERCE': {'THELOOK_ECOMMERCE': ['DISTRIBUTION_CENTERS', 'ORDERS', 'USERS', 'EVENTS', 'INVENTORY_ITEMS', 'PRODUCTS', 'ORDER_ITEMS']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• ORDER_ITEMS."user_id": identify the buyer for every purchase line  
• ORDER_ITEMS."created_at": micro‑seconds timestamp when the item (i.e., the purchase) was created – lets us build a purchase timeline for every user  
• ORDER_ITEMS."status": filter to real purchases (e.g., ‘Complete’ or ‘Shipped’) and ignore cancellations / returns  
• ORDERS."order_id": (optional) cross‑check with ORDER_ITEMS; can also be used to reach the order‑level status  
• ORDERS."created_at": additional timestamp at the order level (often the same as, or very close to, the earliest ORDER_ITEMS."created_at" in that order)  
• USERS."id": user dimension table – helps when we want to count all registered users, join demographics, etc. (not strictly required for the retention calculation)  

Typical conditions that may be useful  
• ORDER_ITEMS."status" IN ('Complete','Shipped','Returned')  -- keep only finished sales  
• ORDER_ITEMS."created_at" < 1672531200000000               -- keep records up to 31‑Dec‑2022 23:59:59 (micro‑seconds)  
• WHERE oi_first."created_at" BETWEEN 1577836800000000 AND 1672444800000000  -- users whose first purchase happened from 01‑Jan‑2020 to 31‑Dec‑2022 (example window)  
• For retention windows we will calculate the difference in months between successive purchases and the user’s first purchase.

Below are 10 incremental Snowflake SQL snippets (each with a short annotation) to inspect the data and finally arrive at the requested retention‑percentage result.  
All identifiers are enclosed in double quotes, queries use simple SELECT only, each finishes with LIMIT 20 so you can preview the intermediate outputs.

```sql
-- 1) Description: Distinct line‑item statuses that exist in ORDER_ITEMS
SELECT DISTINCT "status"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: Distinct order‑level statuses that exist in ORDERS
SELECT DISTINCT "status"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDERS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Sample of ORDER_ITEMS that represent real sales (status <> 'Cancelled')
SELECT *
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"
WHERE "status" <> 'Cancelled'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Sample of orders created before 2023 (micro‑seconds epoch filter)
SELECT "order_id",
       "user_id",
       "created_at",
       "status"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDERS"
WHERE "created_at" < 1672531200000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Find the first purchase (earliest line‑item) for every user up to 2022
SELECT "user_id",
       MIN("created_at") AS "first_purchase_ts"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"
WHERE "status" <> 'Cancelled'
  AND "created_at" < 1672531200000000
GROUP BY "user_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Show first‑purchase month (YYYY‑MM) and number of new purchasers in each month
SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(MIN("created_at")/1000000), 'YYYY-MM') AS "first_purchase_month",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "user_id")                                   AS "new_users"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"
WHERE "status" <> 'Cancelled'
  AND "created_at" < 1672531200000000
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: For every purchase line, calculate the month offset
--    from the user’s first purchase (0 = first month, 1 = second, etc.)
SELECT oi."user_id",
       oi."created_at",
       FLOOR( DATEDIFF('day',
                       TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(fp."first_purchase_ts"/1000000),
                       TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at"/1000000)
                     ) / 30 ) AS "month_offset"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"              oi
JOIN (
      SELECT "user_id",
             MIN("created_at") AS "first_purchase_ts"
      FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"
      WHERE "status" <> 'Cancelled'
        AND "created_at" < 1672531200000000
      GROUP BY "user_id"
     ) fp
  ON oi."user_id" = fp."user_id"
WHERE oi."status" <> 'Cancelled'
  AND oi."created_at" < 1672531200000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Distinct users who purchased in each month_offset (0‑3)
SELECT t."month_offset",
       COUNT(DISTINCT t."user_id") AS "users_in_offset"
FROM (
      SELECT oi."user_id",
             FLOOR( DATEDIFF('day',
                             TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(fp."first_purchase_ts"/1000000),
                             TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at"/1000000)
                           ) / 30 ) AS "month_offset"
      FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
      JOIN (
            SELECT "user_id",
                   MIN("created_at") AS "first_purchase_ts"
            FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"
            WHERE "status" <> 'Cancelled'
              AND "created_at" < 1672531200000000
            GROUP BY "user_id"
           ) fp
        ON oi."user_id" = fp."user_id"
      WHERE oi."status" <> 'Cancelled'
        AND oi."created_at" < 1672531200000000
     ) t
WHERE t."month_offset" BETWEEN 0 AND 3
GROUP BY t."month_offset"
ORDER BY t."month_offset"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Number of new users (cohorts) per first_purchase_month (YYYY‑MM)
--    This will be the denominator for retention percentage
SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(fp."first_purchase_ts"/1000000), 'YYYY-MM') AS "cohort_month",
       COUNT(*)                                                             AS "cohort_size"
FROM (
      SELECT "user_id",
             MIN("created_at") AS "first_purchase_ts"
      FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"
      WHERE "status" <> 'Cancelled'
        AND "created_at" < 1672531200000000
      GROUP BY "user_id"
     ) fp
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: Cohort table showing, for every user‑cohort month, whether
--     they purchased in month 0, 1, 2, or 3 plus the percentage vs cohort size
SELECT cohort."cohort_month",
       off."month_offset",
       COUNT(DISTINCT off."user_id")                                     AS "users_active",
       ROUND( 100.0 * COUNT(DISTINCT off."user_id") / cohort."cohort_size", 2 ) 
                                                                          AS "pct_of_users"
FROM (
      -- cohort set with first purchase month and cohort size
      SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(fp."first_purchase_ts"/1000000), 'YYYY-MM') AS "cohort_month",
             fp."user_id",
             cohort_sizes."cohort_size"
      FROM (
            SELECT "user_id",
                   MIN("created_at") AS "first_purchase_ts"
            FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"
            WHERE "status" <> 'Cancelled'
              AND "created_at" < 1672531200000000
            GROUP BY "user_id"
           ) fp
      JOIN (
            SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(fp2."first_purchase_ts"/1000000), 'YYYY-MM') AS "cohort_month",
                   COUNT(*)                                                             AS "cohort_size"
            FROM (
                  SELECT "user_id",
                         MIN("created_at") AS "first_purchase_ts"
                  FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"
                  WHERE "status" <> 'Cancelled'
                    AND "created_at" < 1672531200000000
                  GROUP BY "user_id"
                 ) fp2
            GROUP BY 1
           ) cohort_sizes
        ON cohort_sizes."cohort_month" = TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(fp."first_purchase_ts"/1000000), 'YYYY-MM')
     ) cohort
JOIN (
      -- every purchase line with its month_offset
      SELECT oi."user_id",
             FLOOR( DATEDIFF('day',
                             TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(fp."first_purchase_ts"/1000000),
                             TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at"/1000000)
                           ) / 30 ) AS "month_offset"
      FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
      JOIN (
            SELECT "user_id",
                   MIN("created_at") AS "first_purchase_ts"
            FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"
            WHERE "status" <> 'Cancelled'
              AND "created_at" < 1672531200000000
            GROUP BY "user_id"
           ) fp
        ON oi."user_id" = fp."user_id"
      WHERE oi."status" <> 'Cancelled'
        AND oi."created_at" < 1672531200000000
     ) off
  ON cohort."user_id" = off."user_id"
WHERE off."month_offset" BETWEEN 0 AND 3
GROUP BY cohort."cohort_month", off."month_offset", cohort."cohort_size"
ORDER BY cohort."cohort_month", off."month_offset"
LIMIT 20;
```

The tenth query returns, for each cohort_month (the month of users’ first purchase), the percentage of those users who went on to make at least one purchase in the 0‑th, 1‑st, 2‑nd, and 3‑rd months after their first purchase – exactly the retention figures requested.
